{"name":"Burnt Sienna","hex":"#a93400","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"burnt sienna","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["dark reddish brown colour, like that of roasted sienna."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a dark reddish brown colour, like that of roasted sienna."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/burnt_sienna"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sienna","blocks":[{"text":"Sienna is an earth pigment containing iron oxide and manganese oxide. In its natural state, it is yellowish brown, and it is called raw sienna. When heated, it becomes a reddish brown, and it is called burnt sienna. It takes its name from the city-state of Siena, where it was produced during the Renaissance. Along with ochre and umber, it was one of the first pigments to be used by humans, and is found in many cave paintings. Since the Renaissance, it has been one of the brown pigments most widely used by artists."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sienna","wikidata":"Q899318"},{"title":"Burnt (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Burnt is a 2015 comedy-drama film directed by John Wells and written by Steven Knight, from a story by Michael Kalesniko. The film stars an ensemble cast including Bradley Cooper, Sienna Miller, Omar Sy, Daniel Brühl, Matthew Rhys, Riccardo Scamarcio, Alicia Vikander, Uma Thurman and Emma Thompson."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/21/Burnt_Poster_Updated.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Burnt_(film)","wikidata":"Q17634968"},{"title":"Burnt Sienna (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Burnt Sienna is the second studio album by Azalia Snail, released in 1992 by Funky Mushroom."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/07/Azalia_Snail_-_Burnt_Sienna.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Burnt_Sienna_(album)","wikidata":"Q5000227"}],"images